{{!--
  The rune circle, shared by the HUD and the GM control panel the way
  `progress-ring.hbs` and `threshold-ladder.hbs` are.

  Expects a circle-shaped context: `runes`, `seatCount`, `seatedCount`,
  `seatRadius`, `circleLabel`, plus `negative` and `complete` from the shared
  card base.

  A seat is one position: one step of the target on a progress or steps track,
  one rung on a threshold ladder. A rune sits in its seat once that position is
  earned and hangs outside the ring until then. Both coordinates come from
  `runeSeats()` in JS, so this template does no arithmetic and CSS is free to
  transition between the two states.

  The runes are HTML spans over an SVG backdrop rather than SVG text, which is
  what keeps `data-tooltip`, focus and text scaling working on them — the same
  reason `threshold-ladder.hbs` places its ticks with `style="left: ...%"`.

  Seating is never carried by position alone: a seated rune is also brighter and
  upright, the active one is ringed, and every rune the reader is allowed to name
  carries that name in its tooltip. The plate is aria-hidden down to the glyphs
  and the wrapper carries the whole accessible name, so a screen reader announces
  "Bind the Wardstone, 3 of 8 runes seated" rather than a row of loose staves.

  Polarity is gated on mode for the same reason the card around it gates it:
  `type` survives a switch to threshold mode, so a track that used to be a
  Negative progress track would otherwise keep painting its runes red while the
  band beside them says otherwise.
--}}
<div class="pvc-runes{{#unless threshold}}{{#if negative}} pvc-runes-negative{{/if}}{{/unless}}{{#if complete}} pvc-runes-complete{{/if}}"
     role="img" aria-label="{{circleLabel}}"
     data-seated="{{seatedCount}}" data-seats="{{seatCount}}">

  <svg class="pvc-runes-plate" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    {{!-- The seat ring itself, so an empty circle still reads as a circle. --}}
    <circle class="pvc-runes-orbit" cx="50" cy="50" r="{{seatRadius}}"/>
  </svg>

  {{#each runes}}
  <span class="pvc-rune{{#if seated}} pvc-rune-seated{{else}} pvc-rune-adrift{{/if}}{{#if active}} pvc-rune-active{{/if}}"
        style="left: {{left}}%; top: {{top}}%; --pvc-rune-turn: {{rotation}}deg"
        data-tooltip="{{tooltip}}" aria-hidden="true">{{glyph}}</span>
  {{/each}}
</div>
